$$

So this point is **not on the unit circle**.

Now, is this point on any segment in $ \mathcal{F} $?

Recall that segments in $ \mathcal{F} $ have length 1, and their endpoints are on the x-axis and y-axis. So we need to check if $ C = \left( \frac{1}{4}, \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \right) $ can be the midpoint of any such segment.

