$$
$$
\frac{b}{2} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \Rightarrow b = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
$$

So the segment is from $ ( \frac{1}{2}, 0 ) $ to $ ( 0, \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} ) $, which is exactly the segment $ \overline{AB} $, and the point $ C = \left( \frac{1}{4}, \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \right) $ is **not on this segment**.

So the point $ C = \left( \frac{1}{4}, \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \right) $ is not on any segment in $ \mathcal{F} $, and it is **not on the unit circle**, and it is **not on the segment $ \overline{AB} $**.

